//
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ Ice Wind Valley V2, the Game Server reads this file instead of IceWindValley.xml when it exists
//~~ Event phases: registration, preparation, siege, end with rewards
//~~ The IGC Client shows registration, siege and ranking windows, the classic client gets chat notices
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### IceWindValley ###
//	Enabled: Deactivates or activates the event: 0/1
//	ServerCode: Server code to run the event on, regular game servers only, see MapServerInfo.xml
//
//	Type: Event registration mode:
//		0: No application required, the first guild master of an eligible guild who enters the castle area during the siege registers his guild
//		1: Registration required via command /regicewind or the registration NPC
//
// ### IceWindValley::Schedule::Start ###
//	DayOfWeek: Day of week the registration starts on
//		~ -1: Every day
//		~ 0: Sunday
//		~ 1: Monday
//		~ 2: Tuesday
//		~ 3: Wednesday
//		~ 4: Thursday
//		~ 5: Friday
//		~ 6: Saturday
//
//	RegHour: Registration hour, 0-23
//	RegMinute: Registration minute, 0-59
//	RegDuration: Time the registration period last, 1-1440 minutes
//	Hour: Start hour of the siege, 0-23, the siege starts at the first such time after the registration ends, also on the next day
//	Minute: Start minute of the siege, 0-59
//	Duration: Siege duration, 1-1440 minutes
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ A Game Server started during the event continues it from the current phase
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### IceWindValley::ApplicationConditions ###
//	MinGuildMember: Minimum guild members to register to the event
//	MaxGuildMember: Maximum guild members to register to the event
//	WCoin: Cost of registration in WCoins
//	GoblinPoint: Cost of registration in Goblin Points
//	Ruud: Cost of registration in Ruud
//	Contribution: Cost of registration in Gens contribution
//	Zen: Cost of registration in Zen
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ The costs are refunded when a registered guild is disbanded before the siege or a Game Master cancels the event
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### IceWindValley::Settings ###
//	EventStartMoveToDevias: Determines move to town mode on event start:
//		~ 0: Do not move
//		~ 1: Move all registered members to Devias 1
//
//	MoveGateID: Gate ID to use for EventStartMoveToDevias option
//	BlockMoveDevias3: If set to 1 the Devias 3 entry will be blocked
//	HideUnregisteredPlayer: Applies invisibility buff for any player not registered to the event, making it unable to disturb the event, 0/1
//	MaxLeaveTime: Time after leaving the throne before the throne time of the guild is lost, see PlayType setting, 1-3600 seconds
//	TotalSitdownTime: Throne time required to win the siege, seconds
//	GuildAssistantCanSit: Determines whether Guild Assistant can sit on throne, 0/1
//	GuildBattleMasterCanSit: Determines whether Guild Battle Master can sit on throne, 0/1, without the setting it takes the value of GuildAssistantCanSit
//	GuildMemberCanSit: Determines whether Guild Member can sit on throne, 0/1
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ Guild master can always sit on throne, GuildAssistantCanSit, GuildBattleMasterCanSit and GuildMemberCanSit apply to both PlayType
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//	PlayType: 
//		~ 0: One throne time of the guild that sat last, after the throne is left only that guild can sit for MaxLeaveTime, then its throne time is lost
//		~ 1: Every guild has its own throne time, any guild can take the free throne, a guild loses its throne time when not sitting for MaxLeaveTime
//
//	VibrationEffect: Deactivates or activates game vibration effect, 0/1
//	VibrationDuration: Vibration effect duration, seconds
//	ApplyFlameEffect: Deactivates or activates flame effect on IceValley castle owners, 0/1
//	TimeoutWinner: Whether or not, the guild with the most throne time wins when the siege time is over, equal time gives no winner, 0/1
//	MoveUnregistered: Players not registered to the event moved out at the siege start:
//		~ Map: Every unregistered player on Devias
//		~ Area: Unregistered players in the castle area
//		~ None: Nobody is moved
//
//	EndSeconds: Time between the end of the siege and the close of the event, 1-120 seconds
//
// ### IceWindValley::Throne ###
//	X: The X coordinate of the throne, the tile a player sits on to take the throne, inside CastleArea
//	Y: The Y coordinate of the throne
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ A player on the throne cannot attack, use skills, warp or use move items, he stands up when he walks
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### IceWindValley::Registration ###
//	NPCIndex: Index of Event Registration NPC, see MonsterList.xml, -1 for no registration NPC
//	MapNumber: Map number of the Registration NPC
//	PosX: The X coordinate of the Registration NPC
//	PosY: The Y coordinate of the Registration NPC
//	Dir: Direction the Registration NPC looks at after spawn
//	Spawn: Whether or not, the Game Server spawns the Registration NPC, 0 uses the NPC of NPCIndex placed at that position in MonsterSpawn.xml, 0/1
//	NpcRange: Maximum distance to the registration NPC to register in the IGC Client window, 1-30 tiles
//	WindowSeconds: Time the IGC Client registration window can be used after talking to the NPC, 10-3600 seconds
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ Use an NPC with no other function, talking to it in the classic client works as command /regicewind
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### IceWindValley::CityLord ###
//	EnableMap: Enables specified map locked to Ice Wind Castle owners
//	Map: Number of map to lock
//	Gate: Gate index to use for the warp, see GateSettings.xml
//	NPC: Index of warp NPC, see MonsterList.xml
//	NPCMap: Index map the NPC is located at, see MapList.xml
//	NPCX: The X coordinate of warp NPC
//	NPCY: The Y coordinate of warp NPC
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ Any NPC can act as the warp NPC for purpose of Ice Valley.
//~~ Original functionality of the NPC will be disabled if defined here.
//~~ The NPC is not being added automatically, must be added manually via MonsterSpawn.xml
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### IceWindValley::CastleArea ###
//	StartX: Start X coordinate of Ice Valley Castle
//	StartY: Start Y coordinate of Ice Valley Castle
//	EndX: End X coordinate of Ice Valley Castle
//	EndY: End Y coordinate of Ice Valley Castle 
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ Coordinates define area within Devias map
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### IceWindValley::Strings::String ###
//	Id: Unique message ID to display for the event
//	Text: Text of the message, order and number of placeholders (%s and %d) must be maintained
//
// ### IceWindValley::RewardsLeader ###
//	EqualWC: Amount of WCoins to reward for guild master of winning guild 
//	EqualGP: Amount of Goblin Points to reward for guild master of winning guild 
//	EqualRuud: Amount of Ruud to reward for guild master of winning guild 
//	EqualContribution: Amount of Gens contribution points to reward for guild master of winning guild 
//	BuffId: ID of buff to apply, see BuffEffectManager.xml::Index
//	BuffDuration: Duration of the buff
//	BuffEffect: Buff Effect ID, see BuffEffectManager.xml::EffectType
//	BuffEffectValue: Buff Effect Value
//	EventBagReward: If set to 1 guild master will be rewarded an item from Event_IWC_GuildMaster.xml bag, the item goes to the Gremory Case
//
// ### IceWindValley::RewardsMember ###
//	EqualWC: Amount of WCoins to reward for guild members of winning guild, read Split description
//	EqualGP: Amount of Goblin Points to reward for guild members of winning guild, read Split description
//	EqualRuud: Amount of Ruud to reward for guild members of winning guild, read Split description
//	EqualContribution: Amount of Gens contribution points to reward for guild members of winning guild, read Split description
//	BuffId: ID of buff to apply, see BuffEffectManager.xml::Index
//	BuffDuration: Duration of the buff
//	BuffEffect: Buff Effect ID, see BuffEffectManager.xml::EffectType
//	BuffEffectValue: Buff Effect Value
//	EventBagReward: If set to 1 guild member will be rewarded an item from Event_IWC_GuildMember.xml bag, the item goes to the Gremory Case
//	Scope: Guild members rewarded:
//		~ Area: Members in the castle area
//		~ Map: Members on Devias
//		~ Online: Members online on the Game Server
//
//	Split: Determines how the amounts are given:
//		~ 0: Every rewarded player gets the full amount
//		~ 1: The amount is divided by the number of rewarded players
//
// ### IceWindValley::RewardsPlayer ###
//	EqualWC: Amount of WCoins to reward for members of registered guilds who lost the event, read Split description
//	EqualGP: Amount of Goblin Points to reward for members of registered guilds who lost the event, read Split description
//	EqualRuud: Amount of Ruud to reward for members of registered guilds who lost the event, read Split description
//	EqualContribution: Amount of Gens contribution points to reward for members of registered guilds who lost the event, read Split description
//	BuffId: ID of buff to apply, see BuffEffectManager.xml::Index
//	BuffDuration: Duration of the buff
//	BuffEffect: Buff Effect ID, see BuffEffectManager.xml::EffectType
//	BuffEffectValue: Buff Effect Value to apply
//	EventBagReward: If set to 1 player will be rewarded an item from Event_IWC_Player.xml bag, the item goes to the Gremory Case
//	Scope: Players rewarded, same values as RewardsMember::Scope
//	Split: Same values as RewardsMember::Split
//
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ The reward buffs must be defined in BuffEffectManager.xml::BuffEffectManager::Period section to apply them as period buffs
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### IceWindValley::Ranking ###
//	RefreshMinutes: How often the ranking window of the IGC Client is read again from the database, 1-1440 minutes
//	Guilds: Number of guilds in the ranking, 1-20
//	Lords: Number of last sieges with their winning guild in the ranking, 1-10
//
// ### IceWindValley::V2 ###
//	Enabled: Whether or not, send the event windows to the IGC Client, 0/1
//
// ### IceWindValley::GmTest ###
//	Times of an event started with the commands of Commands.ini [EventsV2]
//	RegMinutes: Duration of registration, 1-1440 minutes
//	PrepareMinutes: Duration of preparation, 0-1440 minutes
//	DurationMinutes: Duration of the siege, 1-1440 minutes
//
// STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

